  "worked_solution": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1\\ge 0\n$$\n\nSince the inequality ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1\\ge 0$ is true for all values of $x$ and $y,$ the domain of the function $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14246566/assets/402d90507403eabf4cd35cde83a45c9fa2d8080347e1debb0e2463be408b489b.png)",
